{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"The first finding is confirmed in scope. A separate read-authority question remains: with `StepDownOnRemoval=false`, a demoted leader can retain leader state, while the singleton read path checks voter count without checking that the local node is that voter.\n\nThe documented read contract requires application to advance beyond the returned index. I’ll retain that condition and investigate whether a stale read can complete under it.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v1.json'))\nfor b in m['behaviors']:\n if b['id']=='B-apply':\n  b['external_effects']=['When leader, AutoLeave and applied>=pendingConfIndex, appliedTo proposes empty ConfChangeV2. Transfer can reject it; retry requires a later completed application batch or snapshot. Message-only Ready/Advance does not call appliedTo, and transfer timeout only clears leadTransferee.']\n  b['unknowns']=[];b['source_ids']+=['S-transfer-abort']\n if b['id']=='B-read':\n  b['important_branches']=['The singleton branch returns the local committed index without entering the safe-read heartbeat queue; IsSingleton checks one incoming voter and no outgoing voters, not local voter membership.','StepDownOnRemoval=false allows a removed or demoted leader to remain StateLeader. The ReadIndex path has no counterpart of the proposal path local-membership rejection.']\n  b['unknowns']=['Can a demoted leader return an unsafe read barrier after a new singleton leader completes a write, even when the caller later waits until local applied index is strictly greater than the returned index?']\n  b['source_ids']+=['S-singleton','S-stepdown-option','S-read-contract','S-read-entry','S-ready-read-contract','S-config']\nfor p in ['formation','context','connection']:\n x=m['core_overview'][p];objects={o['id']:o for o in m['behaviors']+m['facts']}\n x['source_ids']=sorted(set(x['source_ids']).union(*(set(objects[i]['source_ids']) for i in x['behavior_ids']+x['fact_ids'])))\nm['core_overview']['open_details']=[x for x in m['core_overview']['open_details'] if not x.startswith('Automatic joint-exit')]\nm['core_overview']['open_details'].append('Singleton read authority when the local leader is demoted and optional stepdown is disabled; strict caller application boundary and actual message generation remain to be tested.')\nfor x in m['surfaces']:\n if x['entry_point']=='raft.appliedTo automatic joint exit':x['reason']='Automatic exit after transfer rejection is retried only by later application completion, not transfer timeout or message-only Ready. Scoped result and execution are owned by Candidate 9b1d65cde79f42b59f67880dfd94e0c7 and its assessment.'\nm['surfaces'].append(dict(entry_point='stepLeader singleton ReadIndex after demotion',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-read','B-config'],reason='Singleton cardinality does not establish that the still-leader local instance is its sole voter; demotion can preserve replication participation while optional stepdown is disabled.',source_ids=['S-singleton','S-stepdown-option','S-config','S-proposal'],high_consequence=True))\njson.dump(m,open('map-v1-update.json','w'),indent=2)\nsources=[dict(id='S-singleton',file='tracker/tracker.go',start_line=158,end_line=162,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='S-stepdown-option',file='raft.go',start_line=280,end_line=285,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='S-read-contract',file='node.go',start_line=218,end_line=229,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='S-ready-read-contract',file='node.go',start_line=68,end_line=72,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='S-read-entry',file='rawnode.go',start_line=556,end_line=563,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='S-read-safe-contract',file='raft.go',start_line=58,end_line=71,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='S-removed-leader-test',file='testdata/confchange_v1_remove_leader.txt',start_line=95,end_line=124,kind='test_expectation')]\nq=dict(question='Can a leader demoted to learner with StepDownOnRemoval=false incorrectly use the singleton ReadIndex shortcut and authorize a stale local read after the remaining voter completes a later write, even if the caller advances strictly beyond the returned read index?',importance='Potential violation of the documented ReadOnlySafe linearizable-read responsibility when voter eligibility and retained leader role disagree; no completed stale-read witness exists yet.',source_ids=['S-singleton','S-stepdown-option','S-proposal','S-config','S-read-contract','S-ready-read-contract','S-read-entry','S-read-safe-contract'],participants=['Leader demoted to learner','Remaining singleton voter/new leader','Read caller and replicated state-machine consumer'],objects=['Installed singleton voter configuration','Retained leader role','ReadState.RequestCtx and Index','Already-completed write'],contexts=['ReadOnlySafe','StepDownOnRemoval=false','Joint configuration safely demotes old leader to learner','Network delays keep old leader unaware of new authority when read is admitted'],event_paths=['Commit and apply demotion -> finalize joint change -> isolate demoted leader -> remaining voter elects and commits write -> old leader ReadIndex -> limited later replication advances application past returned index but possibly before write'],activity_classes=['A7','A4','A2','A1'],behavior_ids=['B-read','B-config','B-authority'],fact_ids=['F-config'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B-form':'Legal configuration and later write must be generated and committed through actual quorum operations.','B-apply':'Caller must complete a local read only after application strictly exceeds its returned index.','B-persist':'Ready and transport ordering must preserve generated entries, terms and response provenance.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['StepDownOnRemoval=true steps the demoted leader down and may prevent shortcut access.','A response index below a completed write is not itself a stale completed read: the explicit application boundary must be attained.','Receiving higher-term replication changes the old leader role and drops old-term network responses; the proposed discriminator uses a previously returned local ReadState whose caller has not yet consumed it.','Removed nodes are not automatically assumed to remain valid clients; using a demoted learner retains a documented replication role.'],unknowns=['Can joint demotion finalize with the local role retained using only documented API calls?','Can actual generated, selectively delayed replication satisfy applied>ReadState.Index without applying the previously completed write, after that ReadState was returned locally?','Does another caller rule or consumer invalidate the retained local ReadState on term/role change?'],priority=3,trigger_rationale='Source contrasts explicit membership rejection on proposals with a cardinality-only singleton read shortcut, under an exposed optional-stepdown setting. The public caller contract imposes a strict application boundary, so a controlled legal history is more informative than a direct private-state mutation or a bare low read-index observation. This safety-oriented consumer relationship is selected ahead of the weaker configuration-commit/read-queue reachability suspicion.',disposition='needs_specific_evidence',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')\nchanges={'B-apply':dict(impact='clarification',source_ids=['S-autoleave','S-advance','S-election','S-transfer-abort'],rationale='Replace the answered continuation unknown with the actual conditional trigger relationship. Producer/consumer edges and principal Fact meanings are unchanged.',preserves='C-autoleave-continuation, its legal overlap, dependencies, recurrence observation and review remain applicable; this records its source explanation without changing the proposition.'),'B-read':dict(impact='clarification',source_ids=['S-singleton','S-stepdown-option','S-config','S-read-contract','S-ready-read-contract'],rationale='Expose conditions already inside the mapped singleton read and membership paths. F-config identity and meaning are unchanged; no prior read claim exists.',preserves='The accepted automatic-exit requirement and evidence concern application callbacks, not read authority, and are unaffected.'),'core_overview':dict(impact='clarification',source_ids=['S-autoleave','S-advance','S-singleton','S-config'],rationale='Remove answered automatic-exit reminder and retain the new read-authority discriminator with its strict caller boundary.',preserves='Core formation/context connections and the confirmed automatic-exit claim remain unchanged.')}\nfeedback=dict(ref_ids=['9b1d65cde79f42b59f67880dfd94e0c7','38df82bf7ce148008870835d7e3238d0','B-apply','B-read','F-config','S-autoleave','S-advance','S-singleton','S-stepdown-option','S-ready-read-contract'],answered='The accepted correspondence review confirms the scoped automatic-exit result; the map now records its conditional application-completion retry mechanism. New source investigation distinguishes singleton voter cardinality from local eligibility and retains the stricter applied>read-index consumption contract for a separate read question.',remaining=['Construct a legal demotion/read/replication history and investigate retained local ReadState validity across a subsequent role change.'],understanding='updated',rationale='Record source-level mechanism learning at this related map handoff and select a different responsibility without transferring the earlier execution result to it.')\njson.dump(dict(action='continue',question=q,map_path='map-v1-update.json',map_changes=changes,sources=sources,feedback=feedback,rationale='Investigate a separate safety-oriented read-authority consumer after demotion, with its precise caller and history gaps intact; update answered continuation knowledge at the same natural map handoff.'),open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-06_14-50-17-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
